{{define "server_description"}}
Stash persists agent memory and local work state in namespaces.

Start each session with init. Before history-dependent work, use recall. Store durable decisions, corrections, constraints, project facts, failures, and handoffs with remember; do not store routine narration. Verify a namespace with list_namespaces before writing, and create it when needed. Use context only for short-lived active focus. Episodes are raw observations; facts are consolidated knowledge.

For tracked work, call resume_project with the exact namespace and your routing capabilities. Resume active work first or choose one of the few returned candidates, then call the default brief resume_work. Read the shared goal path and next action, reuse context_digest as known_context_digest, and fetch a linked resource only when it is needed for that action. The full get_goal_map view is for owner monitoring, not routine worker input. Claim the item with claim_work, checkpoint every meaningful result, and use spawn_work when a child or prerequisite is discovered. Attach completion evidence, verify it, and call finish_work only after every required condition and blocker passes. Call handoff_work before ending unfinished work. Git workspace tools are optional connector helpers and are never a prerequisite.

When remember returns indexed=false, the original text is already safe and will be indexed automatically; do not submit a duplicate. Paginated responses may return items, has_more, and next_offset; continue with offset=next_offset. If Stash fails twice, tell the user memory is unavailable instead of pretending it worked.
{{end}}

{{define "init_description"}}
Initialize Stash for this session and idempotently create /, /self, /self/capabilities, /self/limits, and /self/preferences. Call first.
{{end}}

{{define "list_namespaces_description"}}
List available namespaces. Use before choosing a namespace for reads or writes.
{{end}}
{{define "list_namespaces_namespaces"}}
Optional comma-separated paths. A path includes itself and descendants; / means all.
{{end}}

{{define "create_namespace_description"}}
Create a namespace and any missing parents. Check list_namespaces first to avoid duplicates.
{{end}}
{{define "create_namespace_slug"}}
Lowercase path beginning with /; segments may contain letters, numbers, hyphens, and underscores.
{{end}}
{{define "create_namespace_name"}}
Short human-readable namespace name.
{{end}}
{{define "create_namespace_description_param"}}
Specific description that helps future agents choose this namespace.
{{end}}

{{define "remember_description"}}
Store one durable raw observation. If indexed=false, it is saved and automatic indexing is pending; do not resend it.
{{end}}
{{define "remember_content"}}
Self-contained durable information, including enough context to remain useful later.
{{end}}
{{define "remember_namespace"}}
Exact existing namespace path. Defaults to /.
{{end}}

{{define "recall_description"}}
Search episodes and facts by semantic and keyword relevance. Use before history-dependent answers.
{{end}}
{{define "recall_min_score"}}
Optional minimum vector similarity from 0 to 1; 0 disables the filter.
{{end}}
{{define "recall_query"}}
Specific search query using names, identifiers, and relevant terms.
{{end}}
{{define "recall_namespaces"}}
Comma-separated paths to search; each includes descendants. Defaults to /.
{{end}}

{{define "forget_description"}}
Find the closest episode and delete it, or preview with dry_run. Use min_score to avoid deleting an unrelated item.
{{end}}
{{define "forget_min_score"}}
Minimum similarity required for deletion, from 0 to 1. Zero accepts the closest result.
{{end}}
{{define "forget_dry_run"}}
When true, return the match without deleting it.
{{end}}
{{define "forget_about"}}
Description of the episode to find.
{{end}}

{{define "consolidate_description"}}
Derive facts, relationships, patterns, and failure lessons from pending episodes in a namespace.
{{end}}

{{define "set_context_description"}}
Replace the short-lived active focus for one exact namespace.
{{end}}
{{define "set_context_focus"}}
Concise current task, blockers, and next action.
{{end}}
{{define "get_context_description"}}
Read the current short-lived focus for one exact namespace.
{{end}}
{{define "clear_context_description"}}
Remove the current short-lived focus for one exact namespace.
{{end}}

{{define "query_facts_description"}}
List consolidated facts in namespace order. Use recall for relevance-ranked search.
{{end}}
{{define "query_patterns_description"}}
List recurring patterns produced by consolidation.
{{end}}
{{define "query_relationships_description"}}
List relationships between consolidated facts.
{{end}}

